@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# File 10 — Sequential Review Cycle R101–R120 — 2026-09-06
+
+## Governing review discipline
+
+Every numbered round is completed as an uninterrupted, read-only review first. Findings are frozen only after that round is complete. All proven defects from that round are then corrected as one correction phase, followed by full regression/release QA. The next numbered round must not begin until that retest is green.
+
+Governing specification basis: Sabri Social Homeopathy Platform Definitive Master Plan v3.0 and File 10 Video Wall and Live Broadcasting master plan including the Future Video & Broadcasting Intelligence 24 amendment.
+
+Baseline exact reviewed HEAD: `9a2c317d664b3c0d56797afbf1934f6c55479aaa` (`1.2.11-rc1`), with File 10 Release QA run `33353928707` successful.
+
+## R101 — Future-24 implementation reachability and production-studio state reconstruction
+
+**Review completed before correction.** The complete File 10 package was traversed against F10-FR-001..019, F10-NFR-001..010 and F10-FUT-001..024. Future REST routes, production-source/scene/guest/config/simulcast persistence, progressive frontend, object authorization, opaque-ID boundaries, provider-readiness rules and the P0 multi-camera/guest/simulcast/health requirements were reviewed together.
+
+**Frozen finding:** File 10 had canonical mutation paths for production sources, scenes, guest delegation, live policy and simulcast targets, but no owner-scoped canonical read path capable of reconstructing that production state after a reload. The `vwlb_future_production_studio` shortcode also rendered only a capability statement rather than current state. The result was a real end-to-end completeness gap: persisted File 10 production state existed but a broadcaster could not reload it through the versioned opaque-ID REST contract without direct database knowledge.
+
+**Correction:** added `GET /live-events/{id}/production/state` to the canonical Future REST surface. It rechecks the live-event object capability, returns private/no-store data, fails closed with 503 when DB state cannot be verified, excludes native integer IDs/user IDs/credential references, maps scene source membership to opaque public source IDs, and returns safe current sources/scenes/guests/config/simulcast state. The production-studio shortcode now binds to an authorized live event and progressive JavaScript renders current state rather than claiming unconditional provider readiness.
+
+**Regression gate:** `tests/file10-r101-r120-contracts.sh` establishes the R101 read-surface, opaque-ID and UI-state contracts in addition to the complete existing suite.
+
+**Retest:** pending exact-head CI at the time of this ledger commit; the next round may begin only after it is green.
diff --git a/tests/file10-r101-r120-contracts.sh b/tests/file10-r101-r120-contracts.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..5335f59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/file10-r101-r120-contracts.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
+P="$ROOT/video-wall-and-live-broadcasting"
+# R101 — production studio must be reload-safe and must not expose native integer IDs.
+grep -F "production/state','GET','production_state','broadcast'" "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F 'function production_state' "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F 'live_event_public_id' "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F 'source_public_ids' "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F 'Production studio state could not be verified.' "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F 'data-vwlb-production-state' "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-frontend.php" >/dev/null
+grep -F '/production/state' "$P/assets/js/vwlb-future.js" >/dev/null
+# Public DTO query selects must not emit raw live_event_id/user_id/credential refs for the studio-state response.
+python3 - "$P/includes/class-vwlb-future-rest.php" <<'PY'
+import pathlib,re,sys
+text=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text()
+m=re.search(r'public static function production_state\s*\([^)]*\)\s*\{(.*?)\n\t\}',text,re.S)
+assert m, 'production_state missing'
+body=m.group(1)
+for forbidden in ("'user_id'=>", "'live_event_id'=>", "'credential_ref'=>"):
+    assert forbidden not in body, f'raw/internal field leaked in production state: {forbidden}'
+PY
+echo 'R101-R120 contracts PASS'
